{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 30,
    "dDurationMs": 5069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is aerogel.\nThe world's lightest, that is least dense, solid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5700,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This piece has a mass of just 1.22 grams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11580,
    "dDurationMs": 6860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is only a few times the mass of the same volume of air, which kind of makes sense because it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18800,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "99.8% air. In fact, some aerogels are so light that if you removed all the air from them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25330,
    "dDurationMs": 5510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would be less dense than air. I have long been fascinated by aerogel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30840,
    "dDurationMs": 6719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I actually flew out to Aerogel Technologies in Boston to find out why was aerogel invented. How is it made?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37960,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is it such a good thermal insulator and what is it used for?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42190,
    "dDurationMs": 7790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay, we are going to try an experiment to demonstrate the insulating power of aerogel so over here we have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50680,
    "dDurationMs": 6169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two setups: one with a glass petri dish, and the other one with aerogel on top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56860,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Both are made of silica, but with very different physical structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61329,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna see how long it takes to melt these chocolate bunnies with a Bunsen burner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65890,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now to have a look at this experiment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68240,
    "dDurationMs": 5980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have a FLIR T1020 which can see temperatures up to 2,000 degrees Celsius."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74300,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Looks like it's getting pretty hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, you can see that the glass is getting really hot already. And after just a minute:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80140,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's starting to smoke.\n- Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83940,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's definitely melting and smoking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, yeah, here we go. I would say that's phase change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89280,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We've got"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90670,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a liquid chocolate situation. We have some smoking bunny. Over here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94860,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bunny is actually sort of melting over, and look, there, it's sort of tilting to the side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99820,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Alright, I think we're going to call that a melt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103440,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What is that?\n- Oh!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104640,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On cue, on cue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106320,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Laughs.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108720,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I would say that is material fail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Not only did the bunny melt quickly, the petri dish cracked under the thermal expansion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115240,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Wanna pop it in?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115840,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So now let's try the aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118660,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Music]\n- So how is aerogel invented back in?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121340,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Back in 1931, a guy named Professor Samuel Kistler had a bet with his colleague Charles Learned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127600,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now the bet revolved around jellies,\nlike peanut-butter-and-jelly jellies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132700,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the thing about jellies is they are actually a combination of liquids and solids."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137860,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Music]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138360,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, they're mostly liquid,\nbut it's embedded within this 3D solid structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144000,
    "dDurationMs": 5980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So if you think of a gel, like jello, has a skeleton with nano-sized pores that gives it its rigidity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149980,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then that's about 1% of the gel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152580,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the bet was this:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153940,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Could you remove the liquid from the jelly?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157580,
    "dDurationMs": 6110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without affecting the solid structure?\nI mean, if you just evaporate the liquid out, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163690,
    "dDurationMs": 6950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the solid structure shrinks, because as you remove liquid molecules, they pull on each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170640,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they pull on the solid structure around them, basically crumpling it from the inside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176180,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now Samuel Kistler solved this problem in two ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, he realized you could replace one liquid with another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184400,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside the jelly just by washing it thoroughly. So you could swap out, say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189020,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "water, for alcohol. And then, if you take the jelly and put it in a high-pressure vessel called a autoclave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196340,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- By heating it to the high-temperature, high-pressure point called the critical point of the liquid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201680,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that liquid transformed into a semi-liquid, semi-gas called a supercritical fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206680,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- At this point, there is no longer a distinction between liquid and gas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210560,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those molecules are no longer pulling on each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213740,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So once you've depressurized the vessel, that solid skeleton, that 1% of the mass of the gel, is left behind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220960,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intact, except for where there was liquid in the pores before is now gas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225340,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that solid skeleton, that nanoporous solid is what we call aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230100,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Kistler published his findings in Nature in 1931."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234820,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is getting pretty hot as you can see through the thermal camera."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238380,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But coming up on three minutes, there's still no sign of melted chocolate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242340,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're gonna pull out a thermocouple and just check the temperature underneath the bunny."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246440,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, underneath the aerogel, and see what, what the flame temperature is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249640,
    "dDurationMs": 4889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can kind of see that, that parts of the bunny are getting hot, but it's not the bottom of the bunny,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254750,
    "dDurationMs": 2135,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's all the, around the bunny."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256885,
    "dDurationMs": 4175,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Exactly. That convective heat is moving up and around the aerogel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261060,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So you can see the thing is getting red hot.\n- And by four minutes, the bunny is looking a little soft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265180,
    "dDurationMs": 3278,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Still pretty good though, considering how easy it is to melt chocolate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268780,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Can I put my finger here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270920,
    "dDurationMs": 740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Be careful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272980,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not that it's hot, it's that it's brittle.\n- Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277460,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But yeah, totally cool to touch, right?\n- It is, it is just warm to the touch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282120,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- He made aerogels out of all sorts of things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284840,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He made them out of eggs.\nHe made them out of rubber, out of nitrocellulose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289280,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, included in there was silica. Actually right here on the table, I have some examples of some silica gels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296340,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a, a wet silica gel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298840,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's kind of rubbery so I can just,\nyou know, carve out a piece."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302600,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is 97% alcohol inside of its pores."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308300,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the remaining 3% solid is amorphous silica. Just--"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312380,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Can I touch it?\n- Yeah, absolutely. It's kind of rubbery. Not that strong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317180,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So was I cracking it there or was it already kinda cracked?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, you just, no--\n- Oh whoa, it's very easy to break. Very crumbly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322820,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The next step is to replace the alcohol in the gel with liquid carbon dioxide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327280,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We're about to see liquid CO₂."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329540,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Liquid CO₂ has the advantage of being non-flammable, plus it's got a low critical temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334360,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Open it up, and--\n- Yeah, I see it flooding in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336360,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, it's flooding in. There it goes.\nJust another solvent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339760,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Vibration.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340580,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You can clearly see that it's so much cooler on top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345740,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What temperature is it on the bottom?\n- We're at 600 right now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349560,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- 600 degrees Celsius.\n- 600 degrees Celsius, that's 1250 Fahrenheit right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353920,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Notice where the bunny is melting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356180,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's melting right on that edge where the heat's, like, the flame is kind of crawling up and over. - So, yeah, that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362700,
    "dDurationMs": 740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363660,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bunny down! [Laughs.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366260,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, not a bad result.\n- Not a bad result at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370180,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'm interested in in tasting some of this chocolate here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373580,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "( - Gross.)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376720,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Is it hot?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377860,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's warm. \n- Warm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379140,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And delicious.\n- Like fondue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380820,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Mm-hmm. That was great."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383020,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once the liquid CO₂ has filled all the pores of the gel, it's time to take it supercritical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388120,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It was, I would say, a kind of a spiritual experience the first time that I saw a supercritical fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393540,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We'll get to that here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394480,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Laughs.] I love how much you're into these autoclaves.\n- I love aerogels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397940,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make a supercritical fluid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399640,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can heat this with a hairdryer actually."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403260,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Hairdryer blows.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405880,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we approach the critical point, the surface of the liquid becomes kind of blurry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410860,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Weird, huh?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411860,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is like weird waves in there, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414480,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'll speed it up so you can watch the surface disappear altogether."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418580,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're now looking at the supercritical fluid of CO₂."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422720,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this state, the CO₂ can be vented without affecting the solid structure, and what you're left with is aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429020,
    "dDurationMs": 820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "♫"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430440,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you look at aerogel on a light background,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433740,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's almost impossible to see,\nbecause it is pretty transparent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438740,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you look at it on a darker background,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443180,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you can see that it has a slight bluish color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, it's bluish for the same reason that the sky is blue,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451640,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because all those tiny little nanoscale structures,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455360,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they scatter the light according to Rayleigh scattering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, the intensity of light scattered is proportional to\n1 over wavelength to the power of 4,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463560,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means it scatters shorter wavelengths, like blue, much more than it scatters yellow or red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469940,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, for that reason, aerogel looks opaque in the ultraviolet and transparent in the infrared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476760,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now, what do you think this would look like\nif I held it up to the blue sky?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you think we would see?\nWould it look ultra blue?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485720,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, it looks yellow. And that's because the aerogel is actually scattering out that blue light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so what passes through and makes it to our eyes is the longer wavelengths like the yellows and oranges."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498920,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's basically the same effect as looking at a sunset"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502660,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you see the yellows and oranges of a sunset,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's because the blue light\nhas already been scattered out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507440,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the atmosphere the light had to pass through\nbefore it reached your eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512800,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So effectively looking at aerogel against blue sky\nis like looking at a portable sunset."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518380,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The nanoscale pores of the aerogel are also what makes it such a good thermal insulator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523600,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "( - Three.)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527620,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's awesome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528300,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Does that look hot?\n- It's definitely hot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530160,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You might think that because aerogel is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534380,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "largely comprised of air, like 99% air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537780,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it has the same thermal properties as air,\nbut that is not correct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542170,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually a better insulator than air is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545200,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's because the width of the pores is smaller than the distance air molecules travel on average"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550680,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before colliding with something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552420,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their so-called mean free path."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hence, it's really difficult for the hot, fast-moving air molecules below the aerogel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to diffuse through it and transfer heat to the top of the aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563720,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called the Knudsen effect.\n- It is so weird because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568120,
    "dDurationMs": 7940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, you don't expect something that's transparent to block the heat that well, but this really does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576589,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And that's why NASA used aerogel insulation on the Sojourner Rover,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Spirit and Opportunity, the Curiosity Rover, and they plan to use it on future missions to Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587180,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Why does it need insulation?\n- The electronics, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590680,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they don't want the electronics to get cold during the cold nights on Mars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- NASA has also put aerogel to more exotic uses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599240,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "notably to catch dust from a comet\nas part of the Stardust mission."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603220,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the particles were traveling about six kilometers per second relative to the aerogel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608700,
    "dDurationMs": 6380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when they hit the aerogel, because the aerogel's\na very low density material, very, very porous material,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615080,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the particles actually enter the aerogel,\nand as they travel through the aerogel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620580,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they basically break apart the network that makes up the aerogel and they lose energy in the process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626360,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and eventually come to a stop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628120,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is good for capturing particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because if a particle like that were to hit a solid surface then it just stops, you know, immediately."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634440,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It just vaporizes.\n- And vaporizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636620,
    "dDurationMs": 4369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So should we expect to see aerogel in our everyday lives anytime soon?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640989,
    "dDurationMs": 6851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- One of my running jokes is when they build skyscrapers in Antarctica, they'll use aerogel as thermal insulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648240,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Both laugh.]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649640,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Why do you say that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650840,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, because then they'll really care about how,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653660,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just how thermal efficient it is\nbecause it would be so cold there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656680,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657240,
    "dDurationMs": 7660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So instead of having, you know, ten feet of fiberglass insulation, you could have six inches or something of aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665420,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Scientists are currently working on reducing costs and increasing durability."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670060,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And that's true. They do have some elasticity.\n- Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672310,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, so there we go. So it is not hard to break."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676160,
    "dDurationMs": 5389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- They've already made a lot of progress.\nFor example, original silica aerogel is hydrophilic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682160,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There we go. Now this is a hydrophilic aerogel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686020,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So once we've done this, is that piece of aerogel ruined now?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690500,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Pretty much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691340,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But there are ways to make it waterproof."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694240,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to see that and all the other next generation aerogels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698020,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then subscribe to the channel and this may be the start of an aerogel trilogy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703380,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "♫"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706440,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Subtitles credits: 雜碎 Chop Suey, ]\n[Translation credits: ]"
    } ]
  } ]
}
